menu "Regression tests"

config CONF_WITH_REGRESSION_TESTS
    bool "Include built-in regression tests"
    default y
    help
      Build the regression test harness into a separate HD image.
      When enabled, 'make test-hd' produces a raw disk image that
      boots pTOS and runs the test suite automatically.

config CONF_WITH_X86_64_MEMTEST
    bool "Run the x86-64 memory-management self-test at boot"
    depends on MACHINE_PC_X86_64
    default y
    help
      At every boot, exercise the tracked process allocations, the
      growable kernel heap, per-process address spaces and KPROC records
      with repeated create/exit and injected-failure cycles, and check that
      none of them leaks (bios/machine/pc-x86_64/memtest.c).  The result is
      one line on the console, "x86-64 memtest: PASS" or "FAIL (n)", which
      the CI boot test looks for.  It takes a fraction of a second.

config CONF_WITH_X32_ACCESSORY_TEST
    bool "Exercise loaded x32 accessories and desktop restart at boot"
    depends on CONF_WITH_AES && ARCH_X86_64 && CONF_WITH_X86_64_MEMTEST
    depends on CONF_WITH_USER_CALLBACKS
    default n
    help
      Load the four ACC fixtures from make x32-accessory-test, verify
      cooperative message delivery, exit/fault and cancellation, and restart
      the desktop three times while checking tracked resources for leaks.
      Input regressions include real user callbacks revoking registrations
      while keyboard, mouse and timer waits are suspended.

config CONF_WITH_X32_DESKTOP_TEST
    bool "Report external x32 desktop integration checkpoints"
    depends on ARCH_X86_64 && CONF_EXTERNAL_DESK && CONF_WITH_USER_CALLBACKS
    depends on CONF_WITH_READ_INF && CONF_WITH_CLI && CONF_EXTERNAL_CLI
    default n
    help
      Emit serial-only markers from the real desktop for the QEMU PS/2
      integration driver, including CPL, menus, forms and USERDEF drawing.

endmenu
